   standard                     +0.493    +0.475    +0.426    +0.276    +0.084 
  [OK] D1 numerical sensitivity of the alpha1 kernel equals the analytic 1/(2(1+y))
   to fix a0 to 1.8% (2-sigma F-V) from the boost at y ~ 0.3 the boost must be known to 0.7% (sensitivity 0.39), at y ~ 3 to 0.3% (sensitivity 0.14);
   for F-M (4.1%): 1.6% at y ~ 0.3.  The boost must also be independent of the external-field model, the interpolating function and the triple/contamination fraction at that level.
   I make no claim about what DR4 will achieve; the requirement is what any wide-binary analysis would have to beat.
  [OK] D2 the boost is LESS sensitive to a0 than a0 itself is to the data (slope < 0.5 and falling with y): a percent-level a0 needs a sub-percent boost

